Z||000000||KillerX||11-28-2001||01:22 AM||||hello again...sorry for loading the questions, im a moron when it comes to engine and body stuff) but heres all my questions...<P>1) I took out the air box that was in my fiero and i wanted to put in a cold air intake (the cone) but i see alot of stuff i think i should of thought off before taking it off...like 1 is a little plug that was in the air box (what the heck is that! and i think its pritty old and rusty mabey i should get a new one) and second thing i saw was a black metal tube that goes into the air intake close to the throttle where the air goes in...do i need that or can i plug it? ;-)<P>Question 2) Im thinkin about taking my chances on getting the MR2 Kit from erebuni.com and seeing if i can do sumthing to it to make it fit on the fiero and if id doesnt..well i guess im out 500 bux...errr<P>and dinally Question 3) I changed my spark plugs and it was CRAZY black so i went to Crapy Tire and asked whats this from and they said it was running to rich  and it looked like the choke was on...ummmm sure...so i came here and serced  for it but im still lost...<P>thanX guys you guys are a wicked help!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||11-28-2001||03:24 AM||||1a.  That little plug is probably the MAT (manifold air temp) sensor.  Yes, you need it.  Well, kinda.  I've heard you can use a resistor (don't know what value) to trick the comp into thinking the air is colder than it really is, so it richens the mixture.  You can either drill and tap a hole for it into the piping for your CAI, or you can just tie it up somewhere near it.  Not a hugely critical sensor.<P>1b.  That black tube is for the PCV Valve.  I think you can replace that with a small breather (basically a small air filter)<P>2.  Unless you're really really really good with fiberglass and body work you'll be out 500 bucks.  Unless you can turn around and sell it to some dork ricer for 1,000  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>3.  Yes, the black spark plugs were most likely from the engine running way rich.  Which probably means you need a good tuneup.  Plug wires, dist. cap and rotor, oxygen sensor, air filter, fuel filter.. etc.  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedHaze86SD4||11-28-2001||03:18 PM||||I agree with Standard with everything.. On the MR2 Fascia, yes you can, BUT!! You need to use alot of Poly-form type filler and fiberglass to smooth it into the fiero lines.. likely to be too much for you if your not familiar with poly-forming.. Which I know enough about to get me into trouble...<P> Dangit! Wasn't supposed to attach my arm to that!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
